@startuml
!include theme.puml
title Authentication | Login, delegation and refresh reuse
autonumber
actor User
participant "React SPA\nAuthProvider / apiClient" as UI
participant "Nginx gateway" as GW
participant "Identity API" as ID
database identity_db as DB
participant "Domain API" as API
group Login
User -> UI : Submit email/password
activate UI
UI -> GW : POST /api/v1/auth/login
activate GW
GW -> ID : Public login; 5/min IP budget
activate ID
ID -> DB : Platform credential lookup
activate DB
DB --> ID : User record or no match
deactivate DB
ID -> ID : Active + lockout + Argon2 checks
alt Valid credentials
  ID -> DB : Reset failures; INSERT refresh hash + family\nCOMMIT
  activate DB
  DB --> ID : Committed
  deactivate DB
  ID --> GW : 200 access JWT + HttpOnly refresh cookie
else Bad password for an active, unlocked account
  ID -> DB : Increment failures; lock after threshold\nCOMMIT
  activate DB
  DB --> ID : Committed (lockout: default 15 minutes)
  deactivate DB
  ID --> GW : 401 Invalid credentials
else Missing / inactive / locked account
  ID --> GW : 401 Invalid credentials or temporary lockout
end
deactivate ID
GW --> UI : Forward login status, body and issued cookie
deactivate GW
opt Successful login
  UI -> UI : Store access JWT in memory;\nschedule principal lookup through gateway
end
UI --> User : Render authenticated screen or login error
deactivate UI
end
group Protected domain request
activate UI
UI -> GW : Protected request + bearer JWT
activate GW
GW -> ID : Internal auth_request /internal/verify
activate ID
ID --> GW : Verified user/tenant headers or 401
deactivate ID
alt Gateway verification succeeds
  GW -> API : Authorized request + original bearer token
  activate API
  API -> API : Independently verify RS256 / issuer /\naudience / expiry; set tenant DB context
  API --> GW : Domain response or service authorization error
  deactivate API
  GW --> UI : Forward service response
else Gateway verification fails
  GW --> UI : 401; do not dispatch to domain API
end
deactivate GW
deactivate UI
end
group Refresh after a resource response is 401
  activate UI
  UI -> GW : POST /api/v1/auth/refresh + cookie\nsingle in-flight promise per JS runtime
  activate GW
  GW -> ID : Public refresh route
  activate ID
  ID -> DB : Read stored token hash
  activate DB
  DB --> ID : Refresh session or no match
  deactivate DB
  alt Active unexpired refresh token
    ID -> DB : Read linked user
    activate DB
    DB --> ID : User / active status
    deactivate DB
    alt Active user
    ID -> DB : Revoke old row; INSERT successor\nsame family; COMMIT
    activate DB
    DB --> ID : Rotation committed
    deactivate DB
    ID --> GW : 200 new access token + replacement cookie
    else Account unavailable
      ID --> GW : 401 Account unavailable
    end
  else Reused revoked token
    ID -> DB : Revoke active rows in family; COMMIT
    activate DB
    DB --> ID : Family revocation committed
    deactivate DB
    ID --> GW : 401 Session revoked
  else Unknown / expired refresh token
    ID --> GW : 401 Invalid or expired refresh session
  end
  deactivate ID
  GW --> UI : Forward refresh status, body and cookie headers
  deactivate GW
  alt Refresh succeeded
    UI -> UI : Replace in-memory access JWT
    UI -> GW : Retry original request ONCE
    activate GW
    ref over GW,API : Protected-request verification and dispatch above
    GW --> UI : Retried response
    deactivate GW
  else Refresh rejected
    UI -> UI : Session-expired callback;\nProtectedRoute redirects to /login
  end
  deactivate UI
end
note over UI,API
Bars show execution/waiting scopes; dashed arrows return to the caller.
The gateway relays responses; backend APIs do not bypass it.
Principal lookup is routed to Identity, not to a domain service.
A missing refresh cookie is rejected before the token lookup.
Logout revokes the presented refresh row, not every issued access JWT.
Multi-tab refresh coordination is not provided by the single-runtime promise.
Secure-cookie production configuration remains a release gate.
end note
@enduml
